-counting-illegal-immigrants-for-congress-seats", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Occapied Vagina AG and Designated Doobie Inspector Jay Jones Is Fighting a Census Rule That Would Stop Counting Illegal Immigrants for Congress Seats", "last_comment_created": 1794595405208, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 33, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "The Census Bureau proposed counting citizens and lawful permanent residents when it hands out U.S. House seats. Attorney General Jay Jones signed on to a letter calling it \"Trump\u2019s effort to rig the board.\" It was one more Trump fight in a very busy week for his office.", "large_image": "M672RUdVy0mSOfUg.png", "title": "Jay Jones Is Fighting a Census Rule That Would Stop Counting Illegal Immigrants for Congress Seats - Fairfax County Republican Committee"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodjtgHp", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 45, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8938461, "raw_content": "", "author": "flp999", "created": 1794589214190, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "CommieCrats", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATodjtgHp.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/piyH8uzvwQff.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/MStX8lWvcxRXLaXC.jpeg", "width": 588, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 441}], "blurhash": "UXI}x0yY%1D*~p-;V@RjoI%goJbH%MS6WUWX", "full_resolution": [441, 588]}, "title": "Outlook down? GOOD. Everything that\u2019s old is new again, fax is the way.", "last_comment_created": 1794604294617, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 4, "score_up": 45, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATodl0yLS", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 13, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8939022, "raw_content": "Letting Finland into NATO was one of the dumbest strategic blunders of the decade. That country has a military the size of a mid-tier U.S. National Guard unit, a defense budget that wouldn\u2019t even cover a single carrier strike group for a year, and now NATO is stuck with the Alliance\u2019s longest continuous border with Russia thanks to them. All risk, zero real capability.\n\nFinland sat neutral for generations and did just fine. Then the globalist NATO crowd dragged them in, expanding the Alliance right up against Russia\u2019s borders after decades of public assurances that this exact thing would never happen. Broken word. Predictable result: more tension, more money flowing out of American pockets, and another tiny European state that expects U.S. troops and U.S. nukes to underwrite its security while it contributes almost nothing.\n\nKick them out. NATO was never supposed to be a charity for countries that can\u2019t defend themselves. If Finland wants to pick fights on Russia\u2019s doorstep, they can do it with their own limited resources. American blood and treasure are not infinite, and no one owes anyone a blank check for European border games.\n\nMAGA means putting American security and American soldiers first \u2014 not subsidizing every European expansion fantasy. Finland\u2019s membership was a mistake. Reverse it.", "author": "Chukna", "created": 1794613413395, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Chukna", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Letting Finland into NATO was one of the dumbest strategic blunders for the USA", "last_comment_created": 1794615109097, "content": "<p>Letting Finland into NATO was one of the dumbest strategic blunders of the decade. That country has a military the size of a mid-tier U.S. National Guard unit, a defense budget that wouldn\u2019t even cover a single carrier strike group for a year, and now NATO is stuck with the Alliance\u2019s longest continuous border with Russia thanks to them. All risk, zero real capability.</p>\n<p>Finland sat neutral for generations and did just fine. Then the globalist NATO crowd dragged them in, expanding the Alliance right up against Russia\u2019s borders after decades of public assurances that this exact thing would never happen. Broken word. Predictable result: more tension, more money flowing out of American pockets, and another tiny European state that expects U.S. troops and U.S. nukes to underwrite its security while it contributes almost nothing.</p>\n<p>Kick them out. NATO was never supposed to be a charity for countries that can\u2019t defend themselves. If Finland wants to pick fights on Russia\u2019s doorstep, they can do it with their own limited resources. American blood and treasure are not infinite, and no one owes anyone a blank check for European border games.</p>\n<p>MAGA means putting American security and American soldiers first \u2014 not subsidizing every European expansion fantasy. Finland\u2019s membership was a mistake. Reverse it.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 13, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodjuVMp", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 22, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8938753, "raw_content": "", "author": "DefiancetillDeath", "created": 1794603123640, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "JoinTheDiscussion", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.spacex.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATodjuVMp.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.spacex.com/launches/starship-flight-15", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Live: Countdown to Liftoff-Starship\u2019s 15th flight is set to launch later today, Friday, November 13, from Pad 2 at Starbase, Texas. The 75-minute launch window opens at 4:45 p.m. CT.", "last_comment_created": 1794603315397, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 22, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "SpaceX designs, manufactures and launches advanced rockets and spacecraft.", "large_image": "NQ9V44niu7upjvgj.png", "title": "SpaceX"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": 